@startuml
title Bracelet ESP-NOW Packet Flow

participant "Bracelet ESP32-C3" as Bracelet
participant "Station ESP32" as Station

Bracelet -> Bracelet : Read MAC as 6-byte device_id
Bracelet -> Bracelet : Initialize ESP-NOW in WiFi STA mode
Bracelet -> Bracelet : Hop ESP-NOW channels 1..13\nuntil station_control is heard
Bracelet -> Station : bracelet_status broadcast\nprotocol=1, type=1, role=bracelet\nstate, energy, valid_ms, battery_voltage_mv, fault, flags

loop every 200 ms
  Bracelet -> Station : latest 200 ms energy window
end

Station -> Bracelet : station_control optional\nprotocol=1, type=2, role=station\nstation_state, revision, vibration_request, profile
Bracelet -> Station : bracelet_status reply delayed by 100 ms
note right of Bracelet
  station_state values mirror the station enum:
  idle=0, armed=1, ringing=2,
  validating_activity=3, stopped=4, fault=5.
  A received station_control locks the bracelet
  onto that ESP-NOW channel for 15 seconds.
end note

note right of Station
Station remains the alarm authority.
Bracelet energy above threshold mutes alarm
audio for 10 seconds during the station-owned
15-minute activity window.
end note

@enduml
